rge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T05:24:23Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T05:24:23Z","body":"I've added most of these with my best understanding of how to translate them to Godot 4, although I've never worked with multiplayer in Godot so my translations may be off 😅 \r\n\r\nI'm not sure how `master` and `mastersync` would be translated to Godot 4. The [Godot 3 docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/3.6/tutorials/networking/high_level_multiplayer.html) say that \"the `master` keyword means a call can be made from any network puppet to the network master\" but the [Godot 4 docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/networking/high_level_multiplayer.html) say that there are only two modes, one where the authority (master?) can call remotely and one where clients (slaves?) can call remotely.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2788314754/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789159016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104636#issuecomment-2789159016","issue_url":"https://api.gi